  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "xhlU6gAj2BKF75bZouGmchInmfI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:43:57.395Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`@powerhousedao/config` holds the monorepo's configuration package, and its README documents the file every `ph` command reads:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"documentModelsDir\": \"./document-models\",\n  \"editorsDir\": \"./editors\",\n  \"logLevel\": \"verbose\",\n  \"studio\": { \"port\": 3000 },\n  \"reactor\": { \"port\": 4001 },\n  \"packages\": []\n}\n```\n\nThe mechanism is directory-scoped: \"running `ph` commands (like `ph reactor`) from a directory containing a `powerhouse.config.json` will use these values to configure services.\" So the same CLI behaves differently per project without any flags, and a flag is only needed to override the file.\n\nTwo things worth connecting. This is the **same file** Connect's runtime configuration lives in \u2014 its top-level keys (`packages`, `packageRegistryUrl`, `localPackage`) are project-wide and read by ph-cli and the Switchboard too, while the `connect.*` block is Connect-only and passes through the other tools untouched. And the ports here are the source of the numbers seen elsewhere: `reactor.port` 4001 is the switchboard's default listener.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/config/README.md` \u2014 powerhouse.config.json example; Options\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:43:57.395Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:43:57.395Z"
    }
  },
